    "tipsMd": "## Nouns have gender\n\nEvery Spanish noun is masculine or feminine, and the words for \"the\" and \"a\" change to match it.\n\n- Masculine: **el** pan, **un** queso\n- Feminine: **la** leche, **una** manzana\n\n> Learn each noun together with its article. **Agua** is feminine, but it takes **el**: el agua.\n\n## I eat, you eat\n\nThe ending of a verb shows who is doing the action, so **yo** and **tú** are often left out.\n\n- **como** I eat, **comes** you eat\n- **bebo** I drink, **bebes** you drink"
  },
